WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
Mission Impossible.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:04.520
This box will self-destruct in five seconds.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.260
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.080
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.380
And I'm Joe.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.860
Greatest back of the box in the history of the show?

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.860
Did it self-destruct?

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.520
I'm pretty sure one kid in America's copy self-destructed after they read it.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.200
That'd be pretty spooky.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.400
You have to read it, though.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.100
I think that's like a really bad creepypasta.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:54.920
If you don't read the text, you wouldn't know it was happening, so there's no payoff for it.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:01:04.280
So it was like something about like they were using eye tracking software to make sure you read the whole box and then it would self-destruct five seconds after you read the entirety of the box.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.840
And then it's like, I'm right behind you.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:12.500
And the box uses all that same kind of spy language and everything, and they really commit to it.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:25.400
Because even in the manual, there's all sorts of like, not just spy terminology, but just like this whole theme about like a mission briefing throughout the whole thing of like how to use your controller and how the screens work.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.340
Like it's all like it's debriefing you.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:36.300
And I feel like we've seen that before, but I do appreciate the attention to detail here on Mission Impossible, which is obviously, you know, not the movies.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:40.220
This is not the Tom Cruise Mission Impossible thing that hasn't happened yet.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.320
First Mission Impossible movie was like what?

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.120
96? 96, yeah.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:59.140
Yeah. So we're in 1990, but there is a TV show that was out from 88 to 90 that was basically like a revival of the series from the 60s.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.580
So if you're paying attention, we're going backwards.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:01.620
We'll go forward now.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.760
There was a TV series in the 60s.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:07.580
There's a shorter lived TV series in the late 80s.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:16.380
And then now, of course, Mission Impossible is a huge big brand name for Paramount as a movie franchise with Tom Cruise.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.560
Guys, let's start first with the movies since they're the biggest.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:20.920
What's your familiarity with them?

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:25.060
I'm pretty familiar with all of them.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:34.320
I recently marathoned them because, you know, when I was when I was younger, I didn't really know much about them.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.940
But then later, I think it was after maybe Mission Impossible three.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.680
I was I just I got I got into it.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.460
And then after that, I kind of forgot.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:50.460
And then later they just became like action movies without any filler at all.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:53.560
And like that's sort of the case throughout.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.280
And now I just have a deep appreciation for them.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:02.280
And I'm looking forward to the final chapter at some point this year, I think.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:07.120
So as probably a surprise to no one, I'm not super familiar with the franchise.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.600
It is a surprise to me, though, because it seems like this is one where it's just like, how could I have avoided this?

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.120
And it also seems like my type of thing.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.000
I've seen one of the films and it was like one of them.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.940
It was like Mission Impossible six or something.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:22.020
And I saw it in theaters and was like, wow, that was really good.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.520
And then I remember hearing a lot about like a Mission Impossible.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:35.920
The film series does not do what a lot of these other film franchises do and just kind of like get really, really bad over time that like they actually kind of hold a level of quality.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:44.080
And I really do want to binge them and see if that holds true, because I did really like one of these later entries in the movie series.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:51.860
So I've been planning on, you know, it's on my never ending, expanding list of things that I plan on watching that I probably never will.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:04:01.920
Joe, it's funny you bring up about the franchise, not just getting like maybe you were thinking like Fast and the Furious style where it just gets more ridiculous over time.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:07.260
Yeah, that's actually what caught my eye about it was like the directors that are attached to the movies.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:14.260
Like I always associated it as a kid with Tom Cruise, but you've got De Palma, John Woo, J.J.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.560
Abrams, Brad Bird.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:21.340
Like that's pretty impressive lineup of directors continuously attaching themselves to this franchise.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:29.900
Specifically, De Palma was the one that like after I was like the guy who made Blowout and Scarface made a Mission Impossible and it was the first one that I just didn't know.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.420
So I went back and watched it.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.700
And yeah, it's great.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:37.560
It's great stuff. It's the American, the American James Bond kind of.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:38.920
I like that.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:41.080
Yeah, I think that's a that that is a good analogy.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:49.340
It doesn't get as campy as Bond like Bond got really weird in the 80s with that stuff in late 70s.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.760
But it isn't it isn't completely serious.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.440
No, no, it's also very funny series.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:59.320
Right. With the Simon Pegg.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.960
Yes. What was I going to say next?

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:10.080
Oh, but the TV series, though, I had no memory or I feel like I've never seen it on TV.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.440
Like I never found reruns of it or anything.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:18.720
So I wasn't sure if like, well, is that like a serious spy thing or was this like a comedy thing?

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:23.040
Is this like, you know, for me, finding out about Mission Impossible as a TV show.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:34.100
And I'm sorry to make people feel old in this way, but like finding out about Mission Impossible being a TV show was like when I found out 21 Jump Street was also like a TV show before it was the movie.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.700
So I just don't have any attachment to the show.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:38.820
You guys know anything about it?

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:43.500
So did you find this out like while researching for this episode or did you know this before that there was a TV series?

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:48.900
Like I found out about the Mission Impossible TV series while I was like, oh, that's what this is based on.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:52.500
Not the movie. I knew that there was one in like the 60s or 70s.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:54.880
I didn't know that there was one more recently.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:03.240
Same, same. But I think this is like this is like one of those shows that like I feel like I've heard my dad talk about not to not to age my dad here.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:08.260
But yeah, he's old enough to have watched Mission Impossible in the 60s.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:23.760
So, yes, but but yeah, I think he used to talk about some of these and I imagine it was one of the shows again having never seen it, but just from what he's described, I imagine it was taking itself seriously, but maybe difficult to take seriously if we watched it now.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:30.380
But like like the man from uncle or something like that, like one of those types of like it's like silly, but it thinks it's being serious.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.580
Can you confirm Mike?

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:33.400
Like, yeah.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:39.120
Yeah. No, I think that I think Joe's analogy of at the time, it would have been gripping.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:48.660
And now it's like, you know, compared to the more serious spy thrillers or even just like, you know, crime dramas that we have, like it's just like NCIS.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.560
Yeah, just yes, absolutely.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.400
It just doesn't hold up to NCIS.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:05.680
And so, you know, I think this is like one of those, you know, it came in as an as an NES game as the series was ending though, too.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:14.280
So maybe there was like still hopes that like, you know, like the series was just going to continue getting renewed and this would just continue to bring more interest to it.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:19.520
But but I don't know anything about the general plot structure of the show.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:27.760
But I imagine every episode doesn't start with them logging into their computer at work and it's saying good morning, your boss and his secretary have been kidnapped.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:30.020
No, no, no.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:31.900
Which is how the game starts.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:45.420
I do wonder now, like if every episode did have the self-destruct thing, if it was like a like a monster of the week kind of thing or if or if it was more serialized, that that's a good thought.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:46.660
I don't know.

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:59.740
Well, in speaking of this like intro, it also kind of gives that iconic line, which I know from just the movies of your mission, if you choose to accept it is what I always heard.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:00.900
And that's from the movies.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.940
I'm assuming it's similar in the in the TV show.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:09.900
But in here it says your mission, if you decide to accept it, which just I know it's just one minor word difference.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.600
But that just feels so wrong to me.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:12.680
Is that what it was?

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:14.080
It could make all the difference.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:15.600
You're asking the wrong people, Joe.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:28.080
I know. Speaking of speaking of iconic stuff, it also starts with the Mission Impossible theme, which is, you know, obviously famous for the movies now, too, but did exist on the TV show.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:33.880
And Sean, you sung this out last week with that song with the main theme of Mission Impossible.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:39.020
And my favorite rendition of the theme is Sean's version from what episode was that?

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:42.520
It's Mission Impossible in parentheses.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.000
Sean's version. Sean.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.440
Last week's episode was Maniac Mansion.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:47.860
Yeah. The Maniac Mansion.

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:52.240
Sean's version rendition of the Mission Impossible theme is my favorite song of the year.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:53.580
It's good stuff.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:54.780
It's a good song.

00:08:54.780 --> 00:09:05.820
Sean. In the game, you will control a team of three members of the Impossible Missions force, IMF, tasked with rescuing the-

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:16.300
Dr. O. And his secretary, who apparently in the manual maybe, somewhere I read this, is a fellow operative, so it was kind of rude to refer to her as a secretary.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:21.000
Shannon Reed, from the terrorist group Sinister Seven.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.140
Now, come on.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:28.000
What kind of terrorist group just like- that's where it gets like back to the James Bond territory, right?

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:33.680
Of like, Spectre is a little more like ominous than Sinister Seven, right?

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:38.400
Like, this sounds like he's fighting Spider-Man and Electro and Venom and stuff like that.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:43.880
It's just like, it's weird that they went through all the mission debriefing thing and then you take on like, you know, mini-me.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:59.480
I do think this harkens back to a time, which I think it was more like a Cold War thing, where, you know, the enemies of the United States government were more outwardly, like, villainous on purpose.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:06.200
Like, I think this was just a thing, like, and we're- it's just odd to our postmodern ears.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:11.940
You mean they were actually outwardly villainous or were portrayed as more outwardly villainous?

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.960
I'm- I'm- I'm just making shit up, Joe.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:15.640
Okay, I never know.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:24.080
And you play as these- these three members of the IMF via a top-down perspective.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:40.980
Uh, so you have Max, Grant, and Nicholas, and, uh, they can be switched freely, but not in like a Grand Theft Auto V kind of way, where, like, you switch between the three characters and it jumps over to wherever Max was left off or wherever, uh, Grant was left off.

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:47.860
It just switches to them as if they were all three of them were hanging out together going through this mission, and now they just automatically change into-

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.520
Right, like, tagged in.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:54.260
Yeah. Uh, so, say what you will about the actual game and everything.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.760
We'll get into that in a moment, but the first thing I gotta ask you guys is, why are they walking like that?

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.380
I don't know what you mean by like that.

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:08.820
Look- I think if you're gonna make it top-down to- to this extent, this is kind of like what it's gonna look like.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:10.060
Yeah, I think that for me more-

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:11.080
They're doing the Mr.

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:12.460
McMahon shoulder swing.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:18.860
My question was more like, man, why did they go so committed to the top-down?

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:22.400
Like, you could go top-down and be not quite this top-down.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:25.300
I love it. Because it is literally directly overhead.

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:33.740
I'm a little biased because I think what I really like about this visual style is it looks so much like Hotline Miami.

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:42.280
And I think part of that- it also kind of plays like it, like a much more slow Hotline Miami in a way.

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:48.020
But I guess maybe my brain was just used to it from the countless hours of that game that I played.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.080
So this- that didn't bother me that much.

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:52.820
My brain did get used to it over time.

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:56.200
But at first I thought I was playing as like all three Geodudes.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:59.240
Just like their arms and their heads just like bobbing around.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:02.140
Yeah, it's- it's strictly a graphical thing.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:05.280
They do not walk in a way that hinders the gameplay at all.

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:06.660
They are not slow moving.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:13.200
It's a slow-paced game in a way, but they're not walking slow or dragging along or anything.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:17.340
It's just because of how bird's eye we are on this whole thing.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:22.800
They just swing their shoulders very aggressively at times as they're walking around.

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:28.000
And you don't really see like their feet or their knees bending or anything.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:31.140
So it's a little- it's a little strange just to see like that much shoulder swing.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:33.580
So Joe, I like the Geodude analogy.

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:40.800
Now, Max, Grant, and Nicholas wouldn't be interesting if it was just switching between like health-

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.900
available health that they have, right?

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:46.480
Their life meters if you were just like, well, Max is about to die, so I'm just gonna switch into Grant.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:52.040
They, of course, also similar to like how, you know, how we were talking about Castlevania 3.

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.780
Like they all have their own specialization stuff.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.260
So Max is the combat specialist.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.760
Grant is the technical guy.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:03.320
And Nicholas is the master of disguise.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:08.260
And you kind of have to think about the situation you're in and who you want to swap into.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.900
But it's not like if one dies, they all die.

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:15.460
If you lose Nicholas, don't worry, you still have Max and Grant.

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.480
You can be down to just Max.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:20.860
And so therefore, there has to be a way to get around this.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:28.500
It's not like Grant's the only one who can, you know, disarm a bomb or open a gate or something like that.

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:33.060
Are there not instances specifically with Grant where you need him?

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:34.780
That's the only one that I couldn't figure out.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:36.380
Like if I didn't have Grant, how would I get pet?

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:40.800
Because he opens these doors that like I feel like you couldn't open with other characters.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:41.760
Sorry, which one is Grant?

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.440
Grant is the second guy he's got.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:45.860
He punches. The middle guy.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.880
And he can open the coded board doors.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.800
I thought they all could open the coded doors.

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:51.440
I thought I just had to be Grant.

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:52.640
I just kept switching to Grant for those.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:54.760
You can open the... Well, which ones are you talking about?

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:57.620
The ones in the first level or like in general?

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:00.580
Because the ones in the first level, don't they, aren't they like by sound?

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.800
Yeah, but I thought you had to be Grant in order to hear those sounds.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:07.300
Like when I walk up to it as the other guy, it's just a wall.

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:10.140
I had to look it up to figure out how to get through.

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:12.000
Unless I was misunderstanding.

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:14.900
I didn't try it without Grant, so I can't say for certain.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:16.040
I just didn't run.

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:18.660
I didn't hear about any soft locking like that.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:23.700
Yeah, unless I misunderstood it and I was just Grant the whole time after looking it up.

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:28.800
I thought that the first time I went and walked into one of those doors as someone else, I was like, oh, it's just a wall.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:33.600
And then I looked up where do I go and I said, oh, that wall, you use Grant to disarm that wall or something.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:45.800
Interesting. Well, I mean, the other differences between them, I did appreciate that there were actual substantive differences between...

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:54.120
Like Mike mentioned, kind of like the vibes of each, but they all have different weapons, the different sub-weapons.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:58.960
Or I guess in the guy in the rights case, tell me his name.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:00.820
I think it's Nicholas.

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:03.580
Nicholas even has like that...

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:16.180
The one thing that kind of makes it feel like Mission Impossible that isn't the song or the name or the self-destructing, which is like the...

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:17.860
What do you call it?

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:19.060
What do they call that in the movies?

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:31.940
Like camouflage? No, it's like a face maker, which is like making him look like one of the guys and then the AI actually treats him as if there's no enemy there, which I think is really cool.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:45.860
And then they also have different move speeds, which is very important, at least underground in the first level where you keep having to dodge falling sewage.

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:56.680
And so a quick thing, I did not realize how to change between characters, because this is one of those games I did not read the manual for, until pretty late.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:00.680
And I was like, every time I walk by this falling sewage, I get hit.

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.460
So I'm going to die eventually.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:06.500
And then I was like, oh, wait, no, this middle guy walks faster.

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:09.600
So, yeah, they all have their purposes.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.480
Yeah, and I had a similar thing.

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:13.880
I knew how to change the characters.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.540
I just didn't recognize how much quicker Grant walked than the other two.

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:19.920
I just thought, like, I recognized all the other differences.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:23.200
I didn't realize that they had different walk speeds.

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:25.440
So that, I was a little pissed off at first.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:28.720
I was like, what, you just can't get past this waterfall without taking a hit?

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:37.300
And then when I realized, but yeah, I mean, in traversal and in combat, like they each have different weapons where,

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:39.560
and now I'm confusing who has it.

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:43.080
So Nick has the camouflage.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.840
Grant has, like, a stun grenade.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.540
Is that Grant? Yeah, it's like sleepy gas.

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:53.820
Yeah, and that's helpful a lot of times, too, because there are a lot of enemies that are just, like,

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:58.000
constantly firing in one spot that you have to get past.

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:01.100
So, like, you know, that gives you some reason to use Grant.

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:02.560
And then the first guy who...

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:05.920
And luring them out isn't easy, Joe. Like, while we're on that, it's just like, you have to...

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:09.320
They'll stay stubbornly stuck in that spot where they're shooting.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:14.740
Yes. It's not like they have, like, you know, a dedicated ammo that they'll eventually run out of.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.480
You just have to kind of get into their view to have them chase at you.

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:23.380
Otherwise, they will just hide behind that corner continuously shooting at the player.

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:28.660
Right. And then speaking of getting them to chase after you, the other guy, the first guy...

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:30.700
Max. What's his name?

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:31.860
I could do this all day. Max.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:37.920
Max has his, like, detonator bombs where you can, like, get one to chase you, put down

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:39.360
a bomb, and then detonate it at the right moment.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:42.900
Like, and they're all kind of doing similar things, but it's fun.

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:45.640
Yeah, that's how I took care of Riot Shield, guys.

00:17:46.880 --> 00:18:33.780
It's fun. Joe, while you were talking, I took the opportunity to just look up about the Grant thing of it all,

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:35.760
because I do think that's an important detail.

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:40.780
And yes, there are other ways to solve any of these puzzles without Grant,

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:44.040
but Grant is, I don't want to say he's easy mode,

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:47.800
because you're just basically rewarded for keeping him alive, essentially.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:54.300
So, for instance, there's one gate where one side's locked, the other side is not,

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:59.760
and so obviously unlocking it on the left side with Grant will provide an easier path,

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:02.080
whereas the side on the right is a little more perilous.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:06.520
But then there's other things where, like, if you don't have Grant to get this gate open,

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:10.840
you have to, you know, kind of try to find another way in,

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:14.560
and it involves going up a couple floors and then finding a hole,

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:16.940
falling through that hole to get through the area.

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:21.960
So it's a little more like, I'm glad, actually, that that exists.

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:26.540
But I also really like the use of the characters here, where, like, again,

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.580
I don't think Grant is making the game easier.

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:31.380
I think you're being rewarded for keeping these agents alive,

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:34.500
and they should all help you in those kinds of particular ways.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:38.300
But it would suck if Grant was like, you know, you have to get to,

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:42.700
you're on stage five, and you have to make sure that Grant's alive at the very end of the stage,

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.140
or else you can't get to stage six.

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:45.200
Like, that sounds like bullshit.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:51.160
Yeah, yeah. Well, yeah, it's good on them to have not done it that way.

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:52.100
Yeah, that would be a sin.

00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:55.980
Because I feel like a lot of NES games do it that way, where it's like, yeah, you just, you failed.

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:58.760
If that's the case, if that were the case,

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.200
then it would have to be a game over if anybody died,

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.540
or at least, like, a continue situation.

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:11.940
Right. The game stages are not broken into the more traditional, like, action stages in games,

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:14.680
where you just take out enemies and get to the end of a level.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:18.280
You are in, you know, different environments.

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:20.920
One of them is, like, just the streets with civilians,

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:24.320
and others are in, like, the Alps, and so on and so forth.

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:27.240
But all of these different environments require you to kind of, like,

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:30.640
it'd be nice to call them puzzles,

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:35.260
but they're really just, like, different ways of getting through the environments

00:20:35.260 --> 00:20:38.900
that aren't just clear all the enemies in a screen and move along.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:44.120
You're constantly tasked with basically just trying to figure out where you have to go next.

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:47.940
And I think that's especially true in the very first stage of the game.

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:53.220
The very first stage of the game offers a very interesting idea of what the whole game could be,

00:20:53.220 --> 00:20:55.980
in the sense that you are just out on the streets.

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:57.840
There are regular civilians.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:02.220
Unfortunately, the enemies dress exactly the same as the civilians,

00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:04.600
but you're not allowed to kill civilians.

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:08.140
If you do, a helicopter will come and arrest you.

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:10.380
It's a pretty crazy scene.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:12.960
You get down, like, on your knees, hands over your head,

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:16.080
the helicopter comes, and they take that character away.

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:17.480
Your other two agents are free.

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:19.860
Even though they witnessed it, they were right there.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:21.800
It's totally fine.

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:23.460
So if you witness a crime, you should be arrested, Mike?

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:24.680
Yeah, absolutely.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:26.780
They're government agents.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:28.620
They basically coerced them into it.

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:34.640
Anyway, my next point was just going to be that, you know,

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:37.620
it's not inherently obvious, right?

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:41.960
Like, in that first stage, like, oh, I need to go here, then here, then here, right?

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:45.140
Like, a different game would do it that way, but this one doesn't.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:48.620
It's also not obvious, like, what kind of game you're stepping into,

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:53.660
because when I started this first level and I walked into a bar

00:21:53.660 --> 00:22:01.100
and the bartender gave me some info and not every NPC on the screen was trying to kill me.

00:22:01.240 --> 00:22:03.960
I'm like, am I in, like, an immersive sim right now?

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:11.480
Like, is this going to be, like, sort of more open-ended in how I do this?

00:22:11.480 --> 00:22:13.380
And then it very much was not that.

00:22:13.380 --> 00:22:19.300
Like, it's basically just that first screen that feels more lifelike,

00:22:19.300 --> 00:22:23.740
and the rest is, like, video game land.

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:29.540
But, yeah, the information that they give you, it's not complete.

00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:33.520
You end up really having to figure out everything by yourself,

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:37.220
but it's also just a little misleading how the game starts.

00:22:37.220 --> 00:22:43.060
Yeah. Well, and I was also, I mean, just from familiarity minorly with the franchise

00:22:43.060 --> 00:22:48.420
and how it started, I was also surprised with how video game land it became,

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:50.740
where, like, and I was pleased with it.

00:22:50.820 --> 00:22:53.600
I was glad that they didn't, like, take themselves so seriously that, like,

00:22:53.880 --> 00:22:58.240
yeah, we can't have two giant magnets that pull your bullets in one direction.

00:22:58.800 --> 00:23:01.080
Like, that's just, like, fun video gaming stuff,

00:23:01.100 --> 00:23:04.700
and I got to imagine that kind of thing wasn't in the Mission Impossible show,

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:09.080
but as I'm saying that some of those 60s spy shows maybe did have giant magnets

00:23:09.080 --> 00:23:11.920
that were, like, or, like, suits of armors that would, like,

00:23:12.400 --> 00:23:14.420
would swing their swords at you or whatever.

00:23:14.640 --> 00:23:18.920
Like, but having that stuff, or even just the idea of, like,

00:23:19.140 --> 00:23:22.740
there doesn't need to be an explanation as to how you can be Grant

00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:24.860
and then switch to Max and still be the same place,

00:23:24.860 --> 00:23:26.420
and it's like, well, where was Grant before?

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:27.500
Where was Max before?

00:23:27.780 --> 00:23:28.860
Were they in his pocket or whatever?

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:30.260
It's just like, eh, it's a video game.

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:32.600
Just, like, this is how the system works.

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:37.720
And I don't know why I, like, was surprised by that,

00:23:37.780 --> 00:23:40.080
but I just feel like there have been other games where, like,

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:43.600
no, no, no, you've got to go back and get this character now.

00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:46.020
It's, like, just, like, too much work to make it realistic

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:47.160
instead of just make it fun.

00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:50.540
Yeah, and I think there's a lot of fun little set pieces

00:23:50.540 --> 00:23:51.700
throughout the game, too.

00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:54.120
Again, I was trying to, I didn't want to say puzzles

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:55.760
because it's not a puzzle game, right?

00:23:55.840 --> 00:23:58.540
But, like, you have to, like, you're blocked off somewhere,

00:23:58.540 --> 00:24:03.240
so you have to figure out, like, well, where's the off switch on this thing, right?

00:24:03.360 --> 00:24:05.720
Like, how do I get past the next thing?

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:08.000
And you find, you literally find an on-off switch.

00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:09.000
You just have to trigger that.

00:24:09.180 --> 00:24:12.380
Or there's a certain, you know, you need to shut down the power,

00:24:12.500 --> 00:24:13.880
so you've got to look for the power box.

00:24:14.040 --> 00:24:18.600
Like, the game has creative ways of having you explore the levels

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:22.880
without getting too far away from the combat of it all.

00:24:23.220 --> 00:24:26.020
So how is the combat of it all, right?

00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:29.860
If the game is going to stake its name on that, is the combat fun?

00:24:30.120 --> 00:24:31.320
It's simple.

00:24:32.860 --> 00:24:36.680
There's kind of three or four different kinds of enemies

00:24:36.680 --> 00:24:40.580
where you've got, like, a standard, like, melee guy

00:24:40.580 --> 00:24:42.120
that will just rush you.

00:24:42.120 --> 00:24:44.520
You've got gunners.

00:24:44.520 --> 00:24:49.340
You've got these giant Molotov cocktail-throwing guys

00:24:49.340 --> 00:24:52.880
that can really give you some damage.

00:24:52.880 --> 00:24:56.700
Like, I think getting hit by one or just even stepping into the fire

00:24:56.700 --> 00:24:59.380
that they leave behind will cut your health in half.

00:25:00.460 --> 00:25:04.780
And throughout the game, like, there's robots that you've got to avoid

00:25:04.780 --> 00:25:08.120
and, like, the aforementioned suits of armor.

00:25:08.320 --> 00:25:12.180
So there's definitely a good variety of enemy classes.

00:25:12.180 --> 00:25:17.620
It's just those special ones are a bit more rare.

00:25:17.620 --> 00:25:19.520
And the riot shield guy.

00:25:20.360 --> 00:25:27.240
And you'll have to deal with similar enemies throughout the game.

00:25:27.300 --> 00:25:29.520
I'd say it is pretty simple.

00:25:29.700 --> 00:25:31.480
Most enemies only take a hit or two.

00:25:31.940 --> 00:25:37.400
It's more so just finding an angle to get that hit in

00:25:37.400 --> 00:25:40.580
without getting hit yourself like we've been talking about.

00:25:41.980 --> 00:25:44.740
I wouldn't say that there's anything massively wrong with it.

00:25:45.040 --> 00:25:49.040
I wouldn't say that there's really much to really say about the combat

00:25:49.040 --> 00:25:51.340
other than, like, oh, you've got to make sure, like, you know.

00:25:52.600 --> 00:25:54.740
Because also, this top-down thing,

00:25:55.100 --> 00:25:59.780
like, you're shooting from one of your shoulders, basically,

00:25:59.780 --> 00:26:02.680
and you could miss what you think might hit.

00:26:02.880 --> 00:26:04.980
So there's a little bit of a trick to it,

00:26:04.980 --> 00:26:09.040
but no major sins, no major pluses.

00:26:09.520 --> 00:26:13.860
Yeah, I'd say that more so than the way the combat is designed,

00:26:14.140 --> 00:26:17.560
the way that the, I mean, I guess this is combat,

00:26:17.700 --> 00:26:20.980
but the way that the, like, enemy design is around you

00:26:21.940 --> 00:26:23.600
does, for better or for worse,

00:26:23.740 --> 00:26:26.640
make it feel more tactical than a lot of other games

00:26:26.640 --> 00:26:28.240
where it's like, yeah, like you said,

00:26:28.340 --> 00:26:30.080
there's enemies that are shooting at you.

00:26:30.140 --> 00:26:32.360
There's enemies that are, like, sneaking up from around corners,

00:26:32.360 --> 00:26:34.500
and you've got to sort of, like, get the jump on them

00:26:34.500 --> 00:26:35.400
when they're in the right spot,

00:26:35.420 --> 00:26:37.060
where you can hit them and they can't hit you.

00:26:37.120 --> 00:26:38.740
And there's enemies with riot shields

00:26:38.740 --> 00:26:40.180
that are trying to push you off the edge,

00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:42.060
and you've got to kind of get behind them.

00:26:42.260 --> 00:26:44.680
And, you know, all these different little things.

00:26:44.780 --> 00:26:46.480
I mean, there's even, like, if you get caught

00:26:47.220 --> 00:26:49.320
by, like, someone you're talking to

00:26:49.320 --> 00:26:50.740
that turns out to be an enemy,

00:26:50.820 --> 00:26:52.160
or you get caught by, like, a camera or something,

00:26:52.380 --> 00:26:54.420
these, like, giant, like, robot things or something

00:26:54.420 --> 00:26:55.700
with claws come running in,

00:26:55.800 --> 00:26:56.960
and they're, like, really aggressive.

00:26:57.480 --> 00:26:59.340
It's just, there's a lot of different ways

00:26:59.340 --> 00:27:01.240
you have to think about the different enemies,

00:27:02.540 --> 00:27:04.080
which does make it feel,

00:27:05.380 --> 00:27:08.420
I assume intentionally, like, you're this, like, tactician,

00:27:08.420 --> 00:27:10.760
and you've got to decide who's going to take on this battle

00:27:10.760 --> 00:27:12.100
and how am I going to take it on

00:27:12.900 --> 00:27:16.340
in as much as, like, this kind of simple action game can do.

00:27:16.760 --> 00:27:18.940
Why can you shoot the guys with riot shields?

00:27:19.980 --> 00:27:21.340
Because they've got the riot shield.

00:27:21.700 --> 00:27:22.800
Yeah, but I know, but they don't know how,

00:27:23.780 --> 00:27:25.120
it's like three shots,

00:27:25.180 --> 00:27:26.580
and you hit all three of them.

00:27:26.700 --> 00:27:27.820
Like, aren't they supposed to be using the shield

00:27:27.820 --> 00:27:29.180
to bounce off the bullets?

00:27:31.060 --> 00:27:33.280
I think, okay, wait, you're asking

00:27:33.280 --> 00:27:34.840
why can you shoot them?

00:27:34.980 --> 00:27:35.880
Why can you?

00:27:35.980 --> 00:27:37.760
Why can you do damage to those guys?

00:27:37.920 --> 00:27:40.300
I think, like... Can you shoot them from the front?

00:27:40.780 --> 00:27:42.020
Yeah, I did it.

00:27:42.020 --> 00:27:46.100
I think there's one little part of their sprite

00:27:46.620 --> 00:27:48.220
that has a hitbox,

00:27:48.480 --> 00:27:50.620
and the rest of it is shielded,

00:27:50.640 --> 00:27:53.320
because I have been cornered by one

00:27:53.320 --> 00:27:55.640
and just, you know, spammed shoot

00:27:55.640 --> 00:27:58.200
and could not break through.

00:27:58.400 --> 00:27:59.560
I had to, like, lay a bomb.

00:28:00.240 --> 00:28:01.440
I think there might be a little corner.

00:28:01.440 --> 00:28:05.500
Maybe I have to get the head shot. Yeah, that is an exposed shoulder or something.

00:28:07.400 --> 00:28:08.840
But yeah, I also don't want to gloss over

00:28:08.840 --> 00:28:09.700
what you mentioned, Sean,

00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:12.260
speaking of, like, this accuracy thing,

00:28:12.340 --> 00:28:14.540
what you glossed over, or what you mentioned about the...

00:28:15.020 --> 00:28:16.300
The fact that you are shooting

00:28:16.300 --> 00:28:17.900
from, like, one side of your body

00:28:17.900 --> 00:28:19.260
is a little weird,

00:28:19.340 --> 00:28:20.420
because it's like you can never, like,

00:28:20.480 --> 00:28:21.460
line up properly.

00:28:21.680 --> 00:28:22.740
It's never just the thing

00:28:22.740 --> 00:28:23.720
directly in front of you.

00:28:23.760 --> 00:28:24.800
It's always, like, in front of you

00:28:24.800 --> 00:28:25.760
and a little to your right.

00:28:26.420 --> 00:28:28.760
Yeah, because the angle

00:28:28.760 --> 00:28:30.840
that these guys can be standing in,

00:28:30.960 --> 00:28:31.940
it'll just, like,

00:28:31.980 --> 00:28:34.820
oh, your bullet just went right past them,

00:28:34.840 --> 00:28:35.960
but there's no actual way

00:28:35.960 --> 00:28:37.020
to line up the shot otherwise,

00:28:37.080 --> 00:28:38.700
because it's also kind of grid-based.

00:28:39.980 --> 00:28:41.340
It can be tricky.

00:28:41.660 --> 00:28:42.780
That's the word I'll use.

00:28:43.180 --> 00:28:44.000
Yeah, and, like, I know

00:28:44.000 --> 00:28:44.840
they're trying to go for, like,

00:28:44.860 --> 00:28:46.080
oh, he's using his right arm.

00:28:46.160 --> 00:28:47.840
This is more realistic. Like, just have it shoot

00:28:47.840 --> 00:28:48.760
out of the center of his body

00:28:48.760 --> 00:28:50.100
so I can, like, easily see

00:28:50.100 --> 00:28:50.940
where I'm going to shoot.

00:28:51.880 --> 00:28:53.020
I found the game to be

00:28:53.020 --> 00:28:54.680
pretty difficult for...

00:28:54.680 --> 00:28:55.780
because of the enemies.

00:28:56.400 --> 00:28:57.780
I think the combat

00:28:57.780 --> 00:29:00.600
for, like, what your characters are given,

00:29:00.780 --> 00:29:01.980
like, they control well,

00:29:02.180 --> 00:29:03.940
it makes sense, the sub-weapons are good

00:29:03.940 --> 00:29:06.240
and everything, but the enemy placement

00:29:06.240 --> 00:29:07.380
requires a lot of

00:29:07.380 --> 00:29:09.060
forced, closed combat

00:29:09.060 --> 00:29:10.260
in specific levels,

00:29:10.280 --> 00:29:11.380
and I don't think

00:29:11.380 --> 00:29:12.500
it's in a tactical way.

00:29:12.500 --> 00:29:13.320
It's almost in a way

00:29:13.320 --> 00:29:15.780
that's, like, you kind of have to guarantee

00:29:15.780 --> 00:29:17.420
taking a hit or two

00:29:17.420 --> 00:29:18.740
just to even get these guys

00:29:18.740 --> 00:29:20.200
to come out of their spots

00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:21.600
to be able to progress

00:29:21.600 --> 00:29:24.260
around them, and I found that

00:29:24.260 --> 00:29:26.100
to be pretty difficult with the life meter

00:29:26.100 --> 00:29:27.860
and just, like, me personally

00:29:27.860 --> 00:29:29.460
getting through these levels.

00:29:30.680 --> 00:29:31.880
I don't know if, like,

00:29:31.900 --> 00:29:32.980
maybe I just wasn't thinking

00:29:32.980 --> 00:29:35.040
about these combat situations

00:29:35.040 --> 00:29:37.420
correctly, but there were a lot of times

00:29:37.420 --> 00:29:38.960
where, like, you know,

00:29:40.640 --> 00:29:41.740
you are on a bit

00:29:41.740 --> 00:29:42.820
of a linear path

00:29:42.820 --> 00:29:44.640
and to get through you must take out

00:29:44.640 --> 00:29:45.820
these guys because they're shooting

00:29:45.820 --> 00:29:47.180
at you or they're, you know,

00:29:47.300 --> 00:29:48.180
using whatever they have

00:29:48.180 --> 00:29:50.060
on you, and the only way

00:29:50.060 --> 00:29:51.880
to get through is to, you know,

00:29:51.920 --> 00:29:52.780
kind of have them

00:29:53.200 --> 00:29:54.380
get out of those areas

00:29:54.380 --> 00:29:55.220
and chase you down,

00:29:55.300 --> 00:29:56.180
and so you have to kind of, like,

00:29:56.220 --> 00:29:57.640
run over there and bring them back.

00:29:57.640 --> 00:29:58.840
Yeah, you can kind of

00:29:58.840 --> 00:29:59.960
kite some of them.

00:30:00.620 --> 00:30:01.700
If you're playing

00:30:01.700 --> 00:30:03.500
as Glass's guy

